WEBVTT

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:12.262
[grunts]

00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.932
Hold all my calls.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.684
[giggling]

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:19.353
♪ <i>Boss Baby ♪</i>

00:00:19.436 --> 00:00:23.398
<i>♪ I'm the boss, Boss Baby</i>
<i>Boss boss, Boss Baby, boss boss ♪</i>

00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:28.654
<i>♪ Watch a itty-bitty kid get large</i>
<i>I'm the big Boss Baby in charge ♪</i>

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:31.114
♪ <i>Stroller rolling</i>
<i>Up and down the boulevard ♪</i>

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:33.742
<i>♪ I'm the big Boss Baby in charge ♪</i>

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:39.665
<i>♪ I run this house, I rule this crib</i>
<i>Change my diaper, son, where's my bib? ♪</i>

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:42.417
♪ <i>Don't pacify, you just got to pay me ♪</i>

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.962
<i>-♪ Who's in charge? ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Me, the Boss Baby ♪</i>

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:48.423
[grunting]

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.425
You expect me to talk?

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:54.888
I will never betray Planet Earth to you,
Emperor Cavemutant Tentaclemouth!

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:57.599
[speaks gibberish]

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:02.062
Do your worst!

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:05.107
I've seen every nightmare
this galaxy has to-- [gasps]

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.234
What the barf is this garbage?

00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:08.986
[shrieking]

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.280
No!

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.575
For criminy's sake, Tim.
They're not gonna kill you.

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:17.369
Your baby brother likes green beans.
Don't you?

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:19.413
-[coos]
-[Dad laughs]

00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:21.915
You do like them. Yes, you do!

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:23.000
[Mom] Eat up.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:27.796
You have the whole afternoon to play,
but I need to see a clean plate, okay?

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.423
[groaning]

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:33.093
Make me proud, Timmy.
I'm already so proud of you.

00:01:34.678 --> 00:01:37.014
Templeton. Templeton.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:40.309
They're just parents.
You should be playing them like a kazoo.

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:43.562
It's easy for you. You like green beans.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.609
Mm! High fiber with a smooth
grassy flavor. What's not to like?

00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:52.362
-Wait, you could eat my beans.
-Mm, sure could.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:55.198
Mm. Good beans.

00:01:55.282 --> 00:01:58.660
-So...?
-So, what's in it for me?

00:01:58.744 --> 00:01:59.620
What?

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:02.039
-Everything okay in there, boys?
-All good, Dad!

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.290
[giggles]

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:06.418
I'm happy to eat the beans,
but for free? [gasps]

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:10.380
Was there a fire that burned down
the rules of business?

00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:15.469
This isn't a business. We're a family.
We're supposed to--

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:18.639
I don't live in "supposed-ta."
I live in the free market.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:20.223
It's all business.

00:02:20.891 --> 00:02:27.731
Quid pro quo, aka "I doosie, you doosie."
I eat your vegetables, you owe me a favor.

00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:31.818
What favor? Ah, we'll leave it open.
But know this...

00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:35.155
I will collect.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:37.741
Fine. It's a deal.

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:40.285
What?

00:02:40.369 --> 00:02:42.788
Are you trying to choke me,
you homicidal maniac?

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.247
Gotta mash those mammajammas!

00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:47.167
-[Mom] Ready for me to clear plates?
-One more minute!

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:51.171
I bought cookies if you're done!

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:55.050
Mashed! I want it pureed so fine,
it'll be in my diaper by sundown.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:03:00.555
-[Dad] Okay, here comes the cookie-copter!
-Come on, beat it like it owes you money!

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:04.059
[laughs maniacally]

00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:04.976
Good.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.396
[gulps]

00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:10.107
Aww. Who are my two big boys?

00:03:13.068 --> 00:03:16.279
I'm gonna play with the baby.
We're not doing anything suspicious.

00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:17.823
I love you. Bye!

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:22.369
[grunts] Thanks for covering.
I have to check in at the office.

00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:24.162
That mean we're even for the green beans?

00:03:24.246 --> 00:03:26.164
[laughs]

00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:28.834
You know nothing about business.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.335
[laughs, gasps]

00:03:30.419 --> 00:03:33.588
-You should come with me to the office.
-What? Why?

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:35.924
Because we are family.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:39.511
Can't have my brother ignorant
to the art of business. It's embarrassing.

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:41.221
[dinging]

00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:43.682
It'll be fun. I promise.

00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:45.100
I do like fun.

00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:48.145
Do they still have free cookies
in the break room?

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.355
You are literally eating a cookie
right now.

00:03:51.148 --> 00:03:52.274
I'm a kid.

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:54.025
Yes, they have cookies.

00:03:55.444 --> 00:03:57.988
Be advised,
we upgraded the transport chupies.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.531
Do they still work the same way?

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:02.242
-Yes, you suck.
-You suck!

00:04:04.286 --> 00:04:05.704
Ohh.

00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:15.922
Hello, you beautiful Baby Corp.
Let's do some business.

00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:18.633
-[phones ringing]
-[overlapping chatter]

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:23.764
[cries]

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:29.186
-Yo, family man!
-Hey, BB!

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:31.980
Boss Baby!
Still looking for those field reports.

00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:35.025
-On your desk by Friday.
-Outstanding!

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.777
Are they always this friendly?

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.696
That's not friendliness.
It's the halo of success.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.657
Tell me, Templeton,
what do I do here at Baby Corp?

00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:44.409
You make babies?

00:04:44.493 --> 00:04:47.412
Uh, no, the factory downstairs
makes the babies.

00:04:48.079 --> 00:04:51.583
I make sure the world loves babies.

00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:53.710
More than puppies, more than kittens,

00:04:53.794 --> 00:04:56.797
babies get ten times more love
than the competition.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.590
And you know why?

00:04:59.049 --> 00:05:01.301
Uh, I was promised fun and cookies.

00:05:01.384 --> 00:05:02.594
Ah, stay with me.

00:05:02.677 --> 00:05:06.765
It's because of what I've been trying
to tell you. It's all business.

00:05:07.182 --> 00:05:10.477
Baby Corp gives the world
the cuteness it needs.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.649
And in return, the world gives us
what we want. All that love.

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:20.111
Wow, you're great at business.
They should let you run Baby Corp.

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:25.325
-[groans] I tell myself that every day.
-Boss Baby!

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:27.911
Mega Fat CEO Baby.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.871
Good morning, chief!

00:05:29.955 --> 00:05:35.460
Who's crushing it? Numero you-oh! Up high!
But not really. I'm important and busy.

00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:37.254
Great. So we're done here?

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.923
[imitates buzzer] Air ball.
Ask me why I'm busy.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.383
-I'd rather not.
-Why are you busy?

00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:45.220
I'm busy because there's a problem
out in the field, which is what?

00:05:45.303 --> 00:05:48.139
Yeah, your job.
Which I guess you're terrible at?

00:05:48.223 --> 00:05:51.142
Hey! My brother is great at business.

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:55.981
[gasps] Oh, that's right.
You went off and joined a family.

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:57.107
How's that shaking out?

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.483
[laughs]

00:05:58.567 --> 00:05:59.901
Oh, it's shaking fine.

00:06:00.443 --> 00:06:02.946
Yeah, you know what?
My body language don't care.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.699
You wanna bring your man-baby
to the office? Okay.

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:08.493
Makes you look unprofessional and weak,
but whatevs.

00:06:08.577 --> 00:06:11.913
I do appreciate the lecture
on professionalism,

00:06:11.997 --> 00:06:14.833
-but my man-baby is right.
-Can we not call me a man-baby?

00:06:14.916 --> 00:06:17.961
Check the board.
Babies are the most loved creatures

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:20.589
-on the planet.
-Uh-huh, yeah, except...

00:06:20.672 --> 00:06:22.424
Magnus, make it zoom and enhance.

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:26.303
Mega Fat CEO Baby wishes
to zoom and enhance!

00:06:27.637 --> 00:06:31.933
[Mega] Zip. Looky-looky that.
Right in your own town.

00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:35.395
An entire neighborhood
where they don't just not love babies,

00:06:35.478 --> 00:06:37.480
they can't stand babies.

00:06:37.564 --> 00:06:40.775
They hate babies?
What's the problem? Puppy infiltration?

00:06:40.859 --> 00:06:42.819
Worse. A bad baby.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.615
His name is Scooter Buskie.
He's just... [blows raspberry]

00:06:46.698 --> 00:06:48.199
...worst baby in the world.

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:52.203
Scooter Buskie--

00:06:52.287 --> 00:06:53.413
-[thuds]
-[groans]

00:06:55.373 --> 00:06:57.667
-[laughing]
-Scooter Buskie!

00:06:59.628 --> 00:07:01.880
-[man] Huh?
-[all] Scooter Buskie!

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.132
[screams]

00:07:04.215 --> 00:07:05.717
Scooter, no!

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.762
-[woman] Oh, come on!
-[man] Will you please shut your baby up?

00:07:09.346 --> 00:07:11.264
What is wrong with that child?

00:07:11.348 --> 00:07:15.518
The whole neighborhood hates him.
And that's very bad for business.

00:07:15.602 --> 00:07:19.022
[gasps] That poor baby.
We should help him.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.399
Oh, aren't you just a peach, high-tops?

00:07:21.483 --> 00:07:24.486
I'll take care of this Scooter Buskie.

00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:29.449
Uh, yeah, or else. The "else" means
I take this matter to my bosses.

00:07:30.325 --> 00:07:32.410
The Board of Directors.

00:07:32.786 --> 00:07:35.914
And then I get to fire you, so's we clear.
We clear, double-B?

00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:37.290
Yes.

00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:39.250
Sir.

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:42.921
I'm gonna fill my diaper now
and never break eye contact.

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:44.339
-[farts]
-Ooh!

00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:45.340
Smell it!

00:07:45.423 --> 00:07:47.676
Love you, big guy! Not really.

00:07:47.759 --> 00:07:51.805
Mega Fat CEO Baby
does not actually love you.

00:07:51.888 --> 00:07:55.725
We get to go on a secret mission?
You were right. This is fun!

00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:58.561
-Now, where are those free cookies?
-Later.

00:07:58.645 --> 00:08:02.941
We've got a problem baby to deal with.
Time to call in the field team.

00:08:03.024 --> 00:08:04.526
[ringing]

00:08:09.948 --> 00:08:11.992
[Boss Baby] <i>Jimbo, the Muscle.</i>

00:08:15.704 --> 00:08:16.871
[ringing]

00:08:18.373 --> 00:08:20.959
<i>Staci, the Wild Card.</i>

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:24.129
[all grunting]

00:08:24.212 --> 00:08:28.091
<i>The Triplets.</i>
<i>They... mostly stay back at the office.</i>

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:30.218
[loud banging]

00:08:33.805 --> 00:08:34.931
[growls]

00:08:35.807 --> 00:08:36.641
[groaning]

00:08:39.644 --> 00:08:43.231
There you are. Honey, he got out again!

00:08:45.275 --> 00:08:49.237
-Sorry, everyone. He gets out sometimes.
-[muttering]

00:08:51.698 --> 00:08:54.200
Scooter Buskie is a garbage baby.

00:08:54.284 --> 00:08:55.952
Maybe he's just misunderstood.

00:08:57.787 --> 00:09:01.458
Oh, sorry. I didn't realize
your brother was...

00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:02.876
[whispers] ...a liberal.

00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:04.044
-What?
-Shh!

00:09:04.127 --> 00:09:08.548
Triplets, I need a diversion.
Something special from the R&D department.

00:09:10.467 --> 00:09:13.386
-We're helpful!
-[Triplets cheer]

00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:16.723
Jimbo, deliver the package.

00:09:18.516 --> 00:09:20.310
[grunting]

00:09:20.935 --> 00:09:22.395
[rings doorbell]

00:09:25.273 --> 00:09:26.691
[mother] What is it, hon?

00:09:26.775 --> 00:09:29.235
It says we won a free baby swing.

00:09:29.319 --> 00:09:31.529
Ooh, latest model from Japan!

00:09:31.613 --> 00:09:32.614
[mother] Japan?

00:09:32.697 --> 00:09:35.992
-Super-advanced technology.
-Fancy!

00:09:37.952 --> 00:09:40.080
Huh. No assembly instructions.

00:09:40.497 --> 00:09:42.248
-[Jimbo grunts]
-Nice work, Jimbo.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.127
Staci, arrange a meeting.

00:09:54.302 --> 00:09:56.805
Scooter, why are we having
this conversation?

00:09:58.306 --> 00:09:59.933
[belches]

00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:01.309
[snaps fingers]

00:10:01.935 --> 00:10:03.645
Your job is a no-brainer.

00:10:03.728 --> 00:10:06.648
Act cute, Mommy and Daddy
give you food and shelter.

00:10:06.731 --> 00:10:09.484
-You doosie, they doosie.
-[Scooter screams]

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:13.238
How do we move the needle on this one?
Talk to me.

00:10:13.321 --> 00:10:15.240
-[speaks gibberish]
-[all gasp]

00:10:15.323 --> 00:10:16.783
-What did he say?
-Uh...

00:10:16.866 --> 00:10:19.828
Assorted things about our mother.
Better you don't know.

00:10:19.911 --> 00:10:21.871
-[Scooter yelling]
-He's a total loss.

00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:26.126
We issue a factory recall,
take him back to Baby Corp.

00:10:26.709 --> 00:10:30.839
Take him away? You can't.
I thought we were supposed to help him.

00:10:31.422 --> 00:10:35.176
Staci, I like the problem-solving
and lack of morals, but the kid's right.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:38.680
We don't need drastic measures.
What have I been teaching you, Templeton?

00:10:38.763 --> 00:10:42.267
That I owe you a favor? I lost interest
after you promised me cookies.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:46.271
It's all business. We just need
to find out what Scooter Buskie wants.

00:10:46.855 --> 00:10:49.315
Buskie, let's do some business.

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:50.733
[yells]

00:10:50.817 --> 00:10:52.610
That was hard cash, you maniac!

00:10:53.403 --> 00:10:55.780
Maybe this one goes in the...

00:10:55.864 --> 00:10:57.490
[powers up]

00:10:57.574 --> 00:11:00.118
[speaks Japanese]

00:11:01.578 --> 00:11:02.912
-Final offer.
-[squeals]

00:11:03.121 --> 00:11:06.708
Bronze shoes, front row tickets
to Patty Feltmonster's Wiggling Jug Band,

00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:09.794
and we'll throw in
Jimbo's personal stuffed companion.

00:11:09.878 --> 00:11:15.300
Dr. Fluff-Bum... will always love you.
[sobbing]

00:11:15.383 --> 00:11:16.509
[happy squeal]

00:11:17.719 --> 00:11:19.262
[gurgles]

00:11:21.848 --> 00:11:23.182
[all gasp]

00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:29.731
[Scooter screeches]

00:11:29.814 --> 00:11:30.815
[groans]

00:11:30.899 --> 00:11:33.151
It's like negotiating with North Korea!

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:35.904
This is my job on the line.
Somebody help me out!

00:11:35.987 --> 00:11:37.280
[giggles]

00:11:37.363 --> 00:11:38.364
No hugs, Jimbo!

00:11:38.448 --> 00:11:41.451
-You want me to...?
-I do, but think of the lawsuits.

00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:44.162
Maybe not everything's about business.

00:11:44.245 --> 00:11:46.456
You shut your lying mouth!

00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:50.043
If a baby's fussy,
something's probably bothering him.

00:11:50.126 --> 00:11:55.298
What's wrong, widdle grump-grump?
Tummy gurgles? Izzums sweepy?

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:57.508
Doodles in the didee?

00:11:57.592 --> 00:11:59.636
Baby talk is hate speech, Templeton.

00:12:00.219 --> 00:12:01.596
-I got it!
-What?

00:12:01.679 --> 00:12:04.807
See that bump on his gums?
He's getting his first tooth.

00:12:04.891 --> 00:12:09.896
-No wonder poor baby is so cranky.
-Staci, what do we have for tooth pain?

00:12:11.439 --> 00:12:13.900
Frozen pacifier. Numbs the gums.

00:12:18.947 --> 00:12:20.156
All better, Scooter?

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:23.034
I can't believe that worked.

00:12:23.117 --> 00:12:27.163
I brought you to work because I thought
I could teach you something.

00:12:27.246 --> 00:12:29.958
But I was wrong.
You're the one who's teaching me--

00:12:30.041 --> 00:12:32.627
-Fart! Poop! Doody! [shouts]
-[Scooter growling]

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:33.920
Scooter, no!

00:12:34.003 --> 00:12:36.881
That single tooth.
It's like Lucifer's javelin!

00:12:36.965 --> 00:12:38.257
[grunts]

00:12:38.508 --> 00:12:39.676
[Scooter giggles]

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:42.512
[screeches]

00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:44.764
Cool. Now we've added biting.

00:12:44.847 --> 00:12:46.349
Good effort, Templeton.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:50.144
But when you took away Scooter's pain,
all you did was unleash a greater evil.

00:12:50.228 --> 00:12:52.522
-[beeping]
-Sir, the baby-hate is spreading.

00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:56.651
There's a young couple next door
that might actually get a... a cat!

00:12:56.734 --> 00:12:59.487
A cat instead of a baby?

00:12:59.821 --> 00:13:02.824
-[groans]
-Are we gonna get fired?

00:13:03.199 --> 00:13:08.538
No, we are gonna fix this kid.
I've got one last desperate idea.

00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:11.332
Templeton, I'm calling in
that favor you owe me.

00:13:11.416 --> 00:13:12.583
What do you need?

00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:15.878
Gold star stickers.
Go home, grab as many as you can.

00:13:15.962 --> 00:13:18.006
-Meet me at Baby Corp.
-On it!

00:13:20.174 --> 00:13:24.012
-Are you and your brother having fun?
-Nothing suspicious! I love you. Bye!

00:13:25.763 --> 00:13:26.764
Got 'em!

00:13:27.473 --> 00:13:28.474
Outstanding.

00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:32.437
One for Staci. Take one for yourself,
Timmy. You've earned it.

00:13:33.813 --> 00:13:36.524
But what happened
to "one last desperate idea"?

00:13:36.607 --> 00:13:41.029
I'll be honest, Templeton. I decided
to go with Staci's factory recall plan.

00:13:41.112 --> 00:13:44.532
You were against it. Figured I'd save us
an awkward family argument.

00:13:44.615 --> 00:13:47.076
So gold star for me, too. Good job.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.995
What did you do with Scooter?

00:13:49.078 --> 00:13:50.830
We brought him in for retraining.

00:13:51.331 --> 00:13:54.625
<i>♪ Baby, be good</i>
<i>Baby, be good ♪</i>

00:13:54.709 --> 00:13:57.670
<i>♪ Never, never, never, never</i>
<i>Never be bad ♪</i>

00:13:57.754 --> 00:13:59.005
-[shouts] <i>Be good!</i>
<i>-</i>[gasps]

00:13:59.547 --> 00:14:02.300
You just took away that family's baby?

00:14:02.383 --> 00:14:05.344
Of course not.
We gave them a free upgrade.

00:14:05.928 --> 00:14:08.556
What exactly does that mean?

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:11.267
Let me paint you the scene
at the Buskie house.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:12.727
[swing] <i>Turbo! Turbo! Turbo!</i>

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:15.605
[Boss Baby] <i>Right now,</i>
<i>Mrs. Buskie is realizing...</i>

00:14:15.688 --> 00:14:17.607
I should go feed Scooter.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.609
<i>Turbo! Turbo! Turbo!</i>

00:14:19.692 --> 00:14:22.403
[Boss Baby] <i>Can you imagine</i>
<i>that mommy's life, Templeton?</i>

00:14:22.487 --> 00:14:27.241
<i>Every four hours, every day,</i>
<i>she has to feed that... that...</i>

00:14:27.325 --> 00:14:29.285
Scooter Buskie.

00:14:29.369 --> 00:14:33.039
<i>But today is different.</i>
<i>Oh, the routine is the same.</i>

00:14:33.456 --> 00:14:36.626
Scooter, nummy-num time.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:38.544
<i>But what's this?</i>

00:14:38.628 --> 00:14:43.966
<i>When she walks up to that crib,</i>
<i>what precious wonder awaits?</i>

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.385
Scooter?

00:14:45.968 --> 00:14:50.681
A brand-new, powder-clean,
snuggle-hungry baby.

00:14:50.765 --> 00:14:51.933
[giggles]

00:14:52.016 --> 00:14:54.102
<i>She'll be the happiest mommy on Earth.</i>

00:14:54.852 --> 00:14:58.481
[screaming]

00:14:59.524 --> 00:15:02.693
[scoffs] That Buskie baby
is just the worst.

00:15:02.777 --> 00:15:05.613
I'm so glad we opted
for cat ownership instead.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:11.577
What? You are in so much trouble.

00:15:11.661 --> 00:15:13.037
Jimbo's just a fill-in.

00:15:13.121 --> 00:15:16.457
We'll issue the Buskies a factory-fresh
baby as soon as one's available.

00:15:16.541 --> 00:15:20.753
Once Scooter's retrained, we ship him off
to some value-sized mega-family

00:15:20.837 --> 00:15:22.380
who won't even notice the extra kid.

00:15:22.463 --> 00:15:23.923
He'll love Utah.

00:15:24.298 --> 00:15:28.177
It's all business, Templeton.
And I just made this deal a win-win.

00:15:28.761 --> 00:15:34.016
You do not understand families at all!

00:15:34.517 --> 00:15:39.147
-[sighs] Look, maybe this was a mistake.
-So we're taking Scooter back?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:41.649
No, that baby's awful,
and everyone's happier this way.

00:15:41.732 --> 00:15:44.652
-I meant bringing you to the office.
-Oh.

00:15:44.735 --> 00:15:48.656
Don't get me wrong. The brother thing?
I'm still into it 100 percent.

00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:53.119
I just think maybe we keep work at work
and home at home.

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:08.009
I'm gonna say goodbye to Scooter first. 
[laughs]

00:16:08.092 --> 00:16:11.137
-Why the chuckle?
-No reason. I just like laughing.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:12.930
Fine. Knock yourself out.

00:16:15.057 --> 00:16:17.226
<i>♪ Baby be good ♪</i>

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.520
<i>♪ Baby be good</i>
<i>Never, never, never... ♪</i>

00:16:19.604 --> 00:16:21.147
Good baby.

00:16:21.856 --> 00:16:26.319
Bossy B! My main man I just can't stand.
Can I fire you yet?

00:16:26.402 --> 00:16:27.445
[laughs]

00:16:27.528 --> 00:16:30.406
You overpaid kidder.
Staci, call up the charts.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:34.243
You'll find the Buskies' neighborhood
is now one hundred percent...

00:16:35.703 --> 00:16:40.458
It's gonna blow!
Uh... we're gonna make a follow-up visit.

00:16:40.541 --> 00:16:44.212
Just to be sure the Buskies are thrilled
with their baby upgrade.

00:16:44.295 --> 00:16:45.296
[laughs nervously]

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:49.467
[screams] Our baby is missing, there's
a giant muscle-baby in the house,

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:52.178
and why are you still working
on that swing?

00:16:52.261 --> 00:16:55.848
-Scooter's missing?
<i>-Turbo! Turbo! Turbo!</i>

00:16:55.932 --> 00:16:57.475
<i>Turbo! Turbo! Turbo!</i>

00:16:57.558 --> 00:17:00.186
<i>Turbo! Turbo! Turbo! Turbo! Turbo!</i>

00:17:00.269 --> 00:17:02.605
[both screaming]

00:17:03.731 --> 00:17:05.441
-Mama hugs?
-[crashing downstairs]

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.195
So, in summary,
I am on top of things and--

00:17:09.278 --> 00:17:10.738
-[crashing]
-[screams]

00:17:10.988 --> 00:17:12.657
♪ <i>Baby be good ♪</i>

00:17:12.907 --> 00:17:14.408
[screaming]

00:17:14.492 --> 00:17:16.661
-[growling]
-[babies yelling]

00:17:16.827 --> 00:17:18.079
Okay, I'm out.

00:17:18.162 --> 00:17:19.872
[screams]

00:17:19.956 --> 00:17:22.667
And let that teach you a valuable lesson.

00:17:23.543 --> 00:17:24.544
What lesson?

00:17:24.627 --> 00:17:25.586
[screams]

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.756
I will get back to you
when I figure that out.

00:17:28.839 --> 00:17:30.508
[sighs] Come on.

00:17:31.092 --> 00:17:33.010
[growls, gasps]

00:17:36.055 --> 00:17:38.057
[giggles]

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:41.644
-It's headed for the break room!
-Don't let it get sugared up!

00:17:42.812 --> 00:17:44.772
[panicked shouting]

00:17:46.357 --> 00:17:47.900
So he gets cookies?

00:17:50.444 --> 00:17:51.821
[giggles]

00:17:51.904 --> 00:17:56.117
[screeches]

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:57.410
[laughs]

00:18:00.788 --> 00:18:02.873
-[giggles]
-[yells]

00:18:02.957 --> 00:18:05.376
You're not done here after all, Templeton.

00:18:05.459 --> 00:18:08.296
I'll take Staci and deal
with the Jimbo situation.

00:18:08.379 --> 00:18:09.714
That one's on you.

00:18:09.797 --> 00:18:13.634
Um, is there like a security guard or...?

00:18:13.718 --> 00:18:15.261
[whistles] Triplets!

00:18:15.344 --> 00:18:16.846
[Triplets laugh]

00:18:17.471 --> 00:18:18.973
-Yes, boss?
-Reporting for duty!

00:18:19.056 --> 00:18:20.474
Hi, boss's brother.

00:18:20.558 --> 00:18:23.227
Call when you've got him contained.
Don't get me fired!

00:18:24.228 --> 00:18:25.730
I'm a security!

00:18:25.813 --> 00:18:28.941
-[imitates alarm]
-[laughing]

00:18:31.235 --> 00:18:32.278
Goo-goo ga-ga?

00:18:33.487 --> 00:18:38.034
So is the giant muscle-baby working
with the killer robot swing, or...

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:41.162
Who cares?
Get in there and find my little boy!

00:18:42.913 --> 00:18:44.457
What did you do?

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:48.044
Whaaa...?!

00:18:49.128 --> 00:18:51.297
-Scooter! Hey, Scoo--
-[Scooter shrieks]

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.633
Be a good baby! No!

00:18:54.383 --> 00:18:56.260
[Tim] No! Scooter!

00:18:56.344 --> 00:18:58.763
-No! Be a good baby--
-[yelling]

00:18:58.846 --> 00:19:01.515
-[grunts] Huh?
-[alarm dings]

00:19:01.599 --> 00:19:04.393
<i>-Templeton!</i>
-Hey! Everything's under control here.

00:19:04.477 --> 00:19:07.355
<i>You're an atrocious liar.</i>
<i>That's not what I'm calling about.</i>

00:19:07.438 --> 00:19:11.233
<i>The Buskie house is surrounded! Had to</i>
<i>send out the baby swing as a distraction.</i>

00:19:11.317 --> 00:19:13.861
-It's got my gun!
<i>-Turbo! Turbo!</i>

00:19:13.944 --> 00:19:17.073
[Boss Baby] <i>Scan the board</i>
<i>and find us an escape route.</i>

00:19:17.156 --> 00:19:19.825
<i>Tick-tock, Templeton.</i>
<i>The situation is at crisis levels here.</i>

00:19:19.909 --> 00:19:21.410
<i>Staci, how's the neighborhood?</i>

00:19:21.494 --> 00:19:24.205
<i>People are really hating babies, sir.</i>

00:19:24.288 --> 00:19:26.749
-Okay, I have an idea.
-<i>And</i> <i>I have a crisis.</i>

00:19:26.832 --> 00:19:28.709
<i>Winner, me. Where's my escape route?</i>

00:19:28.793 --> 00:19:31.253
[Tim] Oh, Scooter!

00:19:32.546 --> 00:19:35.633
I found more cookies and juice boxes.

00:19:35.716 --> 00:19:36.717
Templeton!

00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:39.553
Templeton, where are you?
I've lost contact.

00:19:39.637 --> 00:19:43.265
Block the door. We get busted,
that's a two-year stretch in daycare.

00:19:43.349 --> 00:19:46.727
No! They can't send me back to daycare.

00:19:46.811 --> 00:19:50.981
[screams] I will go out
in a storm of blood and fire!

00:19:51.065 --> 00:19:53.192
-[Tim] <i>Hey.</i>
-Oh, thank goodness.

00:19:53.275 --> 00:19:54.443
Exit route, Templeton. ASAP!

00:19:54.527 --> 00:19:58.781
<i>Or... since I got Scooter,</i>
<i>I can just send him back to his parents.</i>

00:19:58.864 --> 00:19:59.699
What?

00:19:59.782 --> 00:20:02.368
This situation's a powderkeg,
that baby is the blowtorch.

00:20:02.451 --> 00:20:06.080
Send him out now, no one in
this neighborhood will love babies again!

00:20:06.163 --> 00:20:07.498
I absolutely forbid-- Wait.

00:20:08.082 --> 00:20:10.084
-Where are you right now?
-Too late!

00:20:10.167 --> 00:20:13.087
-[siren wailing]
-[Scooter growls]

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.644
Templeton, you've doomed us all.

00:20:28.728 --> 00:20:30.980
[Scooter growling]

00:20:32.398 --> 00:20:34.817
[all gasping]

00:20:38.362 --> 00:20:40.281
-[snarls]
-Scooter?

00:20:41.073 --> 00:20:43.617
-[giggling]
-[mother laughs]

00:20:43.701 --> 00:20:45.578
Baby boy!

00:20:45.661 --> 00:20:48.581
Oh, come here. My little guy!

00:20:48.664 --> 00:20:50.666
-[excited chatter]
-Hmm?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.418
Aww!

00:20:52.501 --> 00:20:54.086
Aww!

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:55.379
Oh!

00:20:55.463 --> 00:20:59.884
-Babe, let's have a baby!
-I hate cats so much.

00:21:01.594 --> 00:21:05.264
Stand down, boys.
Stand down for sweet, sweet cuteness.

00:21:05.347 --> 00:21:07.224
[swing yells in Japanese]

00:21:07.892 --> 00:21:11.312
Templeton, I am as impressed
as I am mystified.

00:21:11.395 --> 00:21:13.063
It was right on the map.

00:21:13.147 --> 00:21:15.858
The whole neighborhood
hates Scooter Buskie, right?

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:17.818
But not at his house.

00:21:17.902 --> 00:21:21.572
So I figured, you want
to make everyone love babies?

00:21:21.655 --> 00:21:25.326
Maybe they just had to see Scooter
the way his mom and dad do.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:28.871
Not business. Family.

00:21:30.623 --> 00:21:33.375
Sir, baby love is off the charts!

00:21:33.459 --> 00:21:36.337
-I guess it's all over but the cover-up.
-What?

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.963
[siren chirps]

00:21:39.006 --> 00:21:40.633
[Scooter giggles]

00:21:40.716 --> 00:21:41.842
[mother screams]

00:21:41.926 --> 00:21:46.222
-Giant muscle-baby!
-There you are. I am so sorry.

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:48.349
My cousin has wandering baby syndrome.

00:21:48.432 --> 00:21:51.352
It's a real thing that's probably
in the encyclopedia probably.

00:21:51.435 --> 00:21:53.020
Don't check that. I love you. Bye!

00:21:53.813 --> 00:21:55.314
Okay.

00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:58.275
You did good today, Templeton.

00:21:58.359 --> 00:22:02.112
So, uh, do I owe you now?
This is making me uncomfortable.

00:22:02.196 --> 00:22:04.782
Nah, that one was free. We're brothers.

00:22:04.865 --> 00:22:06.283
[laughs]

00:22:06.367 --> 00:22:10.162
-You really know nothing about business.
-And proud of it.

00:22:10.246 --> 00:22:14.500
But you do know family.
That makes us a real synergy powerhouse.

00:22:14.583 --> 00:22:20.214
So maybe if you want,
we could work together again tomorrow?

00:22:20.297 --> 00:22:24.176
Sounds fun.
But this time it's gonna cost you.

00:22:29.974 --> 00:22:31.433
-[screams]
-No, baby!

00:22:33.561 --> 00:22:36.480
Well, I'm full! Gonna go watch TV!

00:22:37.523 --> 00:22:38.857
I love this family.

00:22:38.941 --> 00:22:40.276
[giggles]

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:43.362
[theme song playing]

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:05.551
<i>♪ Boss Baby ♪</i>